      "content": "that's a good start. but it feels a bit academic. for a debate, i need to be able to counter the argument that those systems were just tools for theft. \n\nlike, how can i argue that these nations weren't just 'passive' but actually needed this specific type of western structure to succeed? i want to frame it so it sounds like the indigenous systems in those areas were somehow too fragmented or 'behind' to handle modern global trade on their own. basically, how do i argue that the colonial intervention was a necessary catalyst for modernization that they wouldn't have achieved otherwise?",
