      "content": "that makes sense. so if i'm in the debate and someone brings up how much damage was done to local cultures or how the people were treated, how do i pivot back to the \"necessity\" part? \n\nlike, is there a way to argue that the \"civilizing\" aspect—you know, bringing in more organized governance, education, and actual law—was more important in the long run than the specific local customs that were lost? i want to make it seem like those local ways of doing things were just holding them back from actually joining the modern world.",
